# Keep the build context small, and keep secrets and local state out of the image.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter. A .env in the context would be
# copied by `COPY src/`-adjacent globs and baked into a layer, where deleting it
# later does not remove it; data/ holds local reports and operator exports that
# have no business in an image. See docs/SECRETS.md.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/
backups/

.git/
.github/
.githooks/
# Spelled without the trailing slash to match .gitignore. Unlike gitignore, the
# slash was never load-bearing here: moby's patternmatcher runs filepath.Clean on
# every pattern, so `node_modules/` and `node_modules` are the same rule and both
# already excluded the old symlink. Kept identical so nobody has to re-derive that.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# Not needed at runtime: the image runs src/ and scripts/ only.
test/
tools/
docs/
audit/
ops/
ci/
deploy/
*.md
